<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Santos Zelaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1853">1853</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Santos Zelaya was a Liberal president of Nicaragua from 1893 to 1909. He modernised the state, separated church and state and incorporated the Mosquito Reserve in 1894. A champion of Central American union, he signed the Pact of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amapala">Amapala</a> of 1896. His clashes with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> led to his overthrow in 1909.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-santos-zelaya.jpg" alt="José Santos Zelaya" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jose_Santos_Zelaya_cph.3a03378.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
